* Coaching Star Rating Formula: Blends the specialist attribute with Authority / Level of Discipline, Determination, and Motivation, plus workload (keep all workloads at Light or Average).
* Empirical Hiring Order:
   1. Elite Fitness Coaches First: Cover roughly 46% of match-winning attribute weights and automatically train your Reserve and Youth squads as well.
   2. Physiotherapists & Sports Scientists: Fill all medical slots early (details in Section 6).
   3. Set Piece Coach: Unlocks structured dead-ball execution.
   4. Head of Youth Development (HOYD): Hire primarily for an elite Personality (Model Citizen, Model Professional, Perfectionist, Resolute) and a Preferred Formation matching your first-team shape (visible WWY and coaching tiers barely shift intake CA/PA).
   5. Performance Analysts & Scouts: Prioritise Analysing Data for analysts and Very Good+ regional knowledge, JPA, and JPP for scouts (assign your strongest JPA/JPP staffer to Own Team Reports).
Youth Pathways, Loans & Mentoring
* Board Upgrade Order: Prioritise Junior Coaching and Youth Recruitment ahead of Youth Facilities (Youth Facilities serve hidden pre-intake U16s, whereas controllable U18/U21 squads train in your first-team Training Facilities).
* Age Milestones: Ages 15–17: focus on training workload and physical growth without burning CA on niche traits. Ages 18–21: target roughly 4–5 full matches per month (~125 match points/month). Keep prospects in-house with extra U19/U21 friendlies if needed, or loan 18+ players ONLY to clubs guaranteeing Regular Starter or Important Player status in compatible roles with solid facilities.
* Mentoring Groups (Post-Units Rule): Build compact 3-player downward-only groups led by high-hierarchy, high-Determination/Professionalism Core Social Group seniors to shape hidden personality attributes and traits for mentees under 24. Because FM27 removed legacy senior training units, promote or explicitly add youth prospects to train with the senior squad before adding them to mentoring groups.
5. Matchday Diagnostic, Tactical Tweaks, Shouts & Data Hub
Symptom-to-Response Matchday Diagnostic
Matchday Symptom
	First Diagnostic Question
	Authentic FM27 Response
	Striker isolated / aimless punts
	Are defenders lumping long instead of finding midfield?
	Switch Build-Up to Balanced, Goal Kicks to Short/Mixed to CBs, or toggle Tweaks -> Play Out From the Back.
	Conceding back-post overlaps
	Is an opposing full-back running past our winger?
	Switch AML/AMR OOP role from Wide Outlet Winger (WOW) to Tracking Winger; remove Trap Outside if it invites overlapping crosses.
	Possession without threat
	Are wide players stuck on the touchline with nobody in the box?
	Narrow Attacking Width one notch or toggle Tweaks -> Go Narrower / Swap Wings; verify Three-Man Box runners.
	Played through midfield
	Are CMs pushing too high or facing a narrow 5-man midfield?
	Keep DM intact, shift one CM to Screening Central Midfielder OOP, or adjust Line of Engagement.
	45m–60m stamina dip
	Are low-stamina starters fading after half-time?
	Batch subs cleanly across 2 second-half windows (60m–65m and 75m+) so stoppages are never wasted; use Tweaks -> Take a Breather selectively when stable.
	Protecting a late 1-goal lead (75m+)
	Are we giving away cheap transitions?
	Keep starting CB pairing intact, toggle Tweaks -> Shut Up Shop (late only), and use Shout: Calm Down or Dig Deeper.
	Trailing late (70m–85m+)
	Do we need urgency without losing midfield shape?
	Keep 3 midfielders on pitch, toggle Tweaks -> Play With More Urgency + Swap Wings, and use Shout: Up Your Game or Wake Up.
	FM27 Tactical Tweaks Quick Reference (15 Team + 6 Individual Macros)
Tweaks act as curated one-click macros that stay active until toggled off; they can be stacked (contradictory macros cancel out) and cannot be customised in FM27.


* Build-Up & Directness: Play Out From the Back (vs deep blocks) vs. Go Long (when an aggressive high press pins CBs).
* Tempo & Urgency: Play With More Urgency (trailing) vs. Take a Breather (saves legs when ahead — never trigger too early or it invites sudden AI comebacks).
* Width & Shape: Exploit the Width / Go Narrower / Swap Wings (isolate a tired or booked opposing full-back).
* Pressing: Press Aggressively (target low-Composure/First-Touch defenders) vs. Reduce Pressing (preserve stamina).
* Game-State Extremes: Throw the Kitchen Sink (late desperation) vs. Shut Up Shop / Lock It Down (strictly for protecting a late lead — whole-match use suppresses chances at both ends and costs ~0.20 xPts/game).
* Individual Tweaks (6): GK To Go Up On Set-Pieces (stoppage time only, with fast recovery cover back) plus five role-behavior macros — use Ease Off immediately on yellow-carded aggressive midfielders.
Rebuilt FM27 Shouts & Post-Match Data Hub
* Shouts Modify Mood & Body Language (No Attribute Buffs):
   * Well Done: 2+ goals up or during a dominant spell (avoid praising when drawing).
   * No Pressure: Level scoreline or tight away fixture.
   * Calm Down: Early yellow cards or protecting a narrow 1-goal lead.
   * Up Your Game: Trailing or starting flat.
   * Wake Up: Complacency or immediately after conceding.
   * Dig Deeper: Tired legs grinding out a late result.
* Data Hub Audit Loop: Review Heat Maps, Action Zones, Pass Maps, Shot Maps, and Average Positions (fixed in Patch 27.1.0 to plot players currently on the pitch) alongside high-precision per-90 metrics (xG, NPxG, xA, Open-Play Key Passes, Chances Created, Dribbles, Key Tackles) before making any single tactical adjustment.
6. Medical Centre, Fatigue & PFA Concussion Protocol
Why Physical Readiness Dwarfs Morale on Matchday
FM27's Hawk-Eye movement physics cause Agility, Balance, and Acceleration to fade roughly 10% across 90 minutes, making physical readiness a primary match-winning variable.


* Empirical Cost of Tiredness: Starting an XI at 80% Condition costs roughly 0.80 points per game; 75% Sharpness costs roughly 0.37 points per game; 50% Sharpness costs roughly 1.00 point per game.
* Matchday Selection Rule: While Morale matters off the pitch for dressing-room stability and Player Buy-In, on matchday always favour the fresher, sharper starter over a tired star riding Superb morale.
* Fatigue Monitoring Workflow: Add the Fatigue column to your default Squad View right beside Condition and Sharpness. Manually rest players showing Low or Tired fatigue from training for 2–3 days (Right-click -> Training -> Rest) before hidden jadedness builds up. Use all five substitutions proactively across your 60m–65m and 75m+ windows.
Automatic Training Intensity Caps (Training -> Rest)
* Very Poor Condition: No Pitch/Gym Work (0x)
* Poor Condition: Half Intensity (0.5x)
* Normal Condition: Normal Intensity (1x)
* Good / Superb (Green) Condition Only: Double Intensity (2x)
Clinical Hierarchy, Medical Staff & PFA Concussion Protocol
* Role Specialisation:
   * Head Physio & Physiotherapists (Physiotherapy): Treat existing injuries, shorten recovery times, sharpen return estimates, and run fitness tests/medicals.
   * Sports Scientists (Sports Science): Prevent overuse and recurring injuries, slow jadedness accumulation, and improve Risk Assessment accuracy.
   * Fitness Coaches (Fitness): Develop physical attributes and accelerate post-injury match sharpness recovery across all club squads.
* PFA Concussion Recovery Protocol: Any concussed player must complete the staged recovery pathway and receive explicit neurologist clearance before returning to competitive action.
* Orange vs. Red Injuries (Patch 27.1.0): Red injuries are unavailable; Orange injuries are cleared for light training only and carry high re-aggravation risk if fielded.
* Strict Treatment Rules:
   * Always fund a Specialist for starters and prospects (accelerates recovery and permanently lowers recurring-injury risk).
   * Always Send Home / Isolate viral illnesses or flu to prevent squad-wide outbreaks.
   * Avoid Painkilling Injections outside a cup final or relegation decider (depresses match output while risking severe aggravation and player resentment).
   * Post-Injury Rehab: Assign one of the five Rehab Individual Focuses (Quickness, Agility & Balance, Strength, Endurance, or General Rehab) and rebuild sharpness via 45-minute reserve or substitute outings before full starts.
7. Recruitment Archetypes, Scout Decoding, Contracts & SCR Governance
Five Universal Recruitment Archetypes (+ Goalkeeper Standard)
Recruitment Test: Before signing anyone, ask — Does this player improve the First XI, provide reliable cover, or solve a measured Data Hub gap? Prioritise 2-week free trials, expiring contracts, and low-risk loans when budgets are tight.


1. Goal Threat (ST): Finishing, Composure, Off the Ball, plus Pace/Acceleration or aerial strength (Jumping Reach) fitting the role.
2. Wide Runner (AML/AMR): Pace, Acceleration, Off the Ball, Work Rate, Stamina, and Crossing/Dribbling for dual-phase Tracking Winger work.
3. Midfield Runner / Organiser (DM/MC): Stamina, Work Rate, Decisions, Positioning, First Touch, and Passing to link defence to the box.
4. Defensive Organiser (DC): Positioning, Anticipation, Concentration, Jumping Reach, and Leadership to anchor rest defence.
5. Flexible Full-Back (DL/DR): Defending first (Tackling, Positioning), Stamina, Pace/Acceleration, and clean ball progression.
6. Goalkeeper Standard: Natural GK positional familiarity first, anchored by Agility and Reflexes (highest match-engine weight for shot-stopping).
* Hidden Pressure Check: Value players with "Relishes big matches" and appoint a high-Pressure captain (whose composure partially steadies nervous teammates). Low Pressure triggers pre-match nerves in tough away fixtures and shooting chokes.
Dual-Phase Scouting & Scout Report Decodings
* Scouting Range Discipline: Match Scouting Range to budget (e.g., World / Europe / Domestic only when affordable; drop to Regional/None plus 2-week Free Trials in lower or semi-pro tiers to unmask full attributes for zero cost).
* Recruitment Focuses: Filter by both IP and OOP roles; always check Nearly Matched alongside Matched results.
* Four Crucial Scout Report Signals:
   1. Tactical Effectiveness: Checks immediate IP/OOP system fit (remember teenager Projected Effectiveness remains volatile).
   2. Sell-On Fee Alerts: FM27 surfaces sell-on clauses owed by the selling club directly on the report — explains inflated asking prices upfront.
   3. Injury Proneness Decoder (Hidden 1–20 Scale):
      * No warning = 1–11
      * "Fairly susceptible to injuries" = 12–14
      * "Might have problems with injuries" = 15–17
      * "Could have real problems with injuries" = 18–20
   4. Personality, Consistency & Social Fit: Protects dressing-room Buy-In.
* Transfer Markets: Use TransferRoom Requirements (In) to receive role-matched pitches and TransferRoom Pitch Opportunities (Out) to clear surplus seniors/loanables. Act early on window-long Agent Offers. Use Intermediaries strictly as a last resort for deadwood.
Agreed Playing Time Caps (Strict Rolling ~10-Match Windows)
Always speak to the player's agent before bidding. Use Future Playing Time Pathways and the "Treat club as a stepping stone" promise selectively to beat bigger clubs to young prospects, audit and gently downgrade slipped players every pre-season, and avoid optional promises whenever possible.


Agreed Playing Time Tier
	Rolling ~10-Match Benchmark
	Recommended Squad Cap & Rule
	Star Player
	~90% starts (~9 of 10 games; ~550+ mins)
	Max 1–2 players. Nearly impossible to rotate without rest talks (subbing at HT preserves start credit).
	Important Player
	~75–80% starts (~7 of 10 games; ~400+ mins)
	Max 3–4 players. Core spine starting nearly every league and continental tie.
	Regular Starter
	~65% starts (~5 of 10 games; ~250+ mins)
	6–8 players. Backbone of a balanced rotation squad; absorbs cup rests cleanly.
	Squad Player
	~50–60% involvement (~4 starts per 10; ~200 mins)
	5–7 players. Requires actual starts — bench cameos alone trigger unhappiness.
	Impact Sub
	No start requirement; ~100–150 mins off bench
	3–4 players. Ideal for pacey attackers exploiting late-game Stamina fade.
	Fringe / Breakthrough / Emergency Backup
	Occasional cup starts or injury cover (5–10 apps/season)
	Remaining slots (academy products + veteran 3rd GK). Never over-promise.
	SCR-Safe Contracts, Clauses & Cross-League Regulatory Gates
* Squad Cost Ratio (SCR): Equals Squad Costs (player & head coach wages + transfer amortisation capped at 5 years + agent fees) divided by Adjusted Football Revenue (operating football revenue + net player trading profit; excludes related-party asset sales). Premier League Green cap is 85%, compressing to 70% upon European qualification (aligning with UEFA's 70% cap). Flipping academy graduates and undervalued signings expands the denominator.
* Contract Clause Rules:
   * Build around modest base wages + conditional performance bonuses (Goal, Clean Sheet, Team of the Year, Trophy).
   * Reject or lock out: Match Highest Earner, compounding Yearly Wage Rises, bloated Unused Substitute Fees, and low Minimum Fee Release Clauses (unless legally mandated).
   * Insert club protections: Optional Contract Extension by Club (1–3 years), One-Year Extension After League Games, Top-Division Relegation Wage Drops (promoted clubs), and non-contract appearance deals in semi-pro tiers.
* Key Regulatory Gates for Future Club Moves:
   * Bosman Asymmetry (England): Foreign clubs can sign expiring players on pre-contracts with 6 months left, whereas English clubs cannot approach domestic rivals' players until 1 month before expiry — renew key domestic assets with 18–24 months remaining.
   * GBE & Under-23 ESC Permits (England): Non-UK/Irish players require GBE (FIFA Top-50 caps or 15 points). In FM27, ESC permit slots are restricted to Under-23 players (up to 4 slots PL/Championship, 2 slots League One/Two) — reserve them for difference-making U23 signings, or loan rejected prospects to Belgium/Portugal/Netherlands to farm points.
   * FIFA International Loan Cap: Max 6 over-21, non-club-trained players in or out (max 3 with one club; U21s and club-trained players exempt).
8. Squad Dynamics, Governance & Day-1 New Club Takeover Protocol
Dressing-Room Dynamics & Man-Management Thresholds
* Protect the Core: Guard Team Leaders and your Core Social Group — alienating a leader rallies their social bloc and collapses Atmosphere and Managerial Support. Use supportive captains to defuse teammate grievances.
* Weekly Praise & Criticism Thresholds:
   * Praise weekly training ratings >= 7.1–7.4 directly from the inbox training breakdown and match ratings >= 7.5.
   * Privately criticise weekly training <= 6.5 or poor match ratings <= 6.3.
* Media Handling & Discipline: Evasive and Reserved Media Handling Styles strongly signal high hidden Professionalism. Automated Code of Conduct fines apply strictly to objective offences (red cards, suspension bans, missed training) — fining for poor match performances remains permanently removed. Delegate routine weekly press conferences to a high-Motivation Assistant Manager; handle derbies, title deciders, and board-pressure moments personally.
Bobby Dean's Upgraded Day-1 New Club Takeover Protocol (Any Future Club)
1. PC Workflow & Save Hygiene: Verify Continue Flow (Balanced or Custom), Information Display density (unlocked for 1080p+ in Patch 27.1.0), Secondary Navigation Landing Spots, Bookmark Bar, and store saves outside OneDrive sync.
2. Audit Before Changing: Switch Squad view to Contracts to flag expiring deals, dangerous clauses, and excess Star Player statuses; verify wage cap / SCR headroom, medical risks, and backroom staff balance before bidding on anyone.
3. Set Staff Responsibilities Deliberately: Keep manual control of Senior General Training, Individual Training, First-Team Transfers/Contracts, Set Pieces, and Matchday Tactics/Tweaks; delegate routine pressers and youth friendlies.
4. Fit Squad to Principles: Map the best natural XI to the 4-3-3 IP / 4-1-4-1 OOP roles via the Combined view, verify every phase shift in the 3x3 Tactics Visualiser, and keep Tactical Complexity modest early.
5. Upgrade Staff by Empirical Impact & Badges: Hire elite Fitness Coaches first, followed by Physios, Sports Scientists, Set Piece Coach, high-personality HOYD, and Analysts/Scouts; request your next coaching licence once board confidence and finances stabilise.
6. Lock Training, Medical & Mentoring Rhythm: Designate 1 Primary Trained Tactic, schedule ~8 Tactical Understanding blocks/month on Chance Creation, Pressing Intensity, and OOP Shape until starters exceed 51, protect post-match full Rest days, set conservative automatic intensity caps, add Fatigue to Squad View, and set up 3-player downward-only mentoring groups.
7. Launch Dual-Phase Scouting, Affiliates & Day-1 Dynamics: Right-size Scouting Range (or use 2-week Free Trials), launch IP/OOP Recruitment Focuses, request a strategic Affiliate (Senior Affiliate for free loans/fee in lower tiers; Youth/Work Permit affiliates higher up), and deliver an encouraging Day-1 Team Meeting aligned to realistic targets.
8. Enforce Five-Game Block Decision Gates:
   * Block 1 (MD1–5): Stability, familiarity building, and baseline match evidence.
   * Block 2 (MD6–15): Attacking efficiency and Home vs. Away structural audit.
   * Mid-Season Window: Contract renewals and 1–2 targeted gap fixes — never a panic rebuild.
   * Run-In: Pragmatism, late-game Tweaks discipline, and ruthless fatigue management.